  "behavior": [
    "Non-default dependency-free avro feature; core/default companion dependency graphs and lockfiles unchanged.",
    "Borrowed explicit writer/reader root JSON and flattened resolved named-reference sets are bounded together before codec resolution; empty inputs and duplicate names within either set fail before codec entry.",
    "Caller-selected Codec resolves writer/reader schemas once and retains immutable selections; defaults, unions, named references, promotions and compatibility are explicit codec responsibilities.",
    "Encoding obtains exact writer-schema datum length, checks overflow/frame limit before allocation, reserves one bounded frame fallibly, and supplies only its exact payload slice.",
    "Decode borrows the bounded frame payload and rejects unknown writer IDs before entering the codec. Reported partial writes and incomplete/over-reported consumption cannot return success.",
    "Structured input/header/schema-ID/length/size/reservation failures preserve selected codec failures. No schema text or payload is embedded in adapter diagnostics.",
    "No registry lookup, registration, compatibility policy or reference traversal is implicit; raw Avro datums use Confluent five-byte framing, including an empty datum for primitive null."
